# ───── Man-page Style Help ─────────────────────────────
read -r -d '' 'MSG[help_text]' <<'EOF'
NAME
    Proton Drive Backup

DESCRIPTION
    One-way backup tool for local directories and files with the remote
    Proton Drive storage, including upload of new/changed files, and
    deletion of orphaned remote files. The local system is the single
    source of truth; no local deletions are executed.
    Change detection is based on local MD5 checksum comparison against
    a persistent database. No remote hash data is required.
    This is an unofficial community tool. Proton AG is not responsible
    for its functionality or maintenance. Proton Drive is a trademark
    of Proton AG.

REQUIREMENTS
    - proton-drive CLI v0.4.6 or higher
    - jq (JSON processor)
    - md5sum (checksum utility)
    - bash version 4.0 or higher
    - tar

USAGE
    %s [OPTIONS]

    OPTIONS
        --dry-run     Display changes, no action taken.
        --help        Show this help and exit.
        --log         Open and follow runtime log; quit with Ctrl+C + Q.
        --quiet       Run backup silently (for cron jobs).
                      Console output: errors and summary only.
        --reset-db    Reset checksum database and rebuild.
        --schedule    Auto-schedule the cronjob
                      (every %s minutes).
        --unschedule  Remove the cronjob.
        --verbose     Run backup with progress indicator.
        --version     Show version information.

LOGGING
    Log file  %s
    Rotation  Internal, run-based, logs archived with the next run.
              %s rotated logs kept, oldest deleted).

DELETE STRATEGY
    Current mode  %s
    Options       "trash" (recoverable) or
                  "delete" (permanent).
    Configure via DELETE_MODE variable in config file.

DISCLAIMER
    This script is provided "as is"; there is NO WARRANTY at all. Use at
    your own risk. Licensed under the MIT License.

AUTHOR
    Copyright (c) 2026 RML Tec Dev
    (not affiliated with Proton AG)
    rmltecdev@pm.me
EOF

MSG[help_close]="Help closed."
MSG[help_open]="Opening help..."

